namespace com.trustblocks.identity@1.0.0

/**
 * credentialSubject shapes for the Verifiable Credentials this app issues
 * -- see com.trustblocks.did.vc. Not a contract model: nothing here is
 * `identified`, because nothing here is stored as a first-class asset in
 * its own right. A credential's identity is the signed JWT itself
 * (com.trustblocks.xtdb.credential keys its XTDB record by the same id
 * the VC's own `id`/subject+type carries); these concepts only shape what
 * one credential's `credentialSubject` may say.
 *
 * The outer W3C envelope ($id, issuer, validFrom/validUntil, proof) is
 * not modeled here at all, deliberately -- it is JSON-LD, open-world by
 * design, and it is what com.trustblocks.did.vc/issue builds directly.
 * Concerto is closed-world (see trustblocks-templates' docs/templatemark-conformance.md and the
 * trigger endpoint's own request validation for two other places this
 * project has already leaned on that), which is exactly right for a
 * `credentialSubject` -- a specific, finite claim -- and exactly wrong
 * for a spec whose whole point is that anyone can add a term.
 *
 * `id` on every concept below is the subject's own DID string --
 * `credentialSubject.id` in W3C terms, spelled the same here as there on
 * purpose, so nothing translates one name to another crossing that
 * boundary.
 */

enum Authority {
  o CERTIFY_MINUTES
  o ATTEST_ORDINANCES
  o SIGN_CONTRACTS
  o ATTEST_FINANCIALS
  // A construction contract's pay applications -- see
  // docs/design/matters.md's first slice.
  o RECEIVE_PAY_APPLICATIONS
  o RECEIVE_INSPECTION_REPORTS
  o CERTIFY_INSPECTIONS
  o CERTIFY_PAY_APPLICATIONS
  o APPROVE_PAYMENTS
  o CERTIFY_PAYMENTS
  // The finance forms a matter's package names -- vendor forms, W-9s,
  // insurance certificates, E-Verify affidavits -- received by the Finance
  // Director (trustblocks-templates' packages/street-resurfacing).
  o RECEIVE_FINANCE_FORMS
  // Advisory only: to sign an Advisory on a matter's documents. The one
  // authority an AI agent can be designated -- see Advisory.
  o ADVISE
}

/**
 * "Town Clerk" is not its own identity -- it is this claim, issued by the
 * Town to a person's did:key. See trustblocks-templates' docs/model-conventions.md's
 * reuse-by-inheritance rule for why a role lives as data here rather than
 * as a type: an OfficeGrant is not a MunicipalAgreement's concern, and an
 * officeholder is not a party the way a contract's signatories are: they
 * act *for* the town, not as a counterparty to it.
 */
concept OfficeGrant {
  o String id
  o String name
  o String office
  o Authority[] authority
}

/**
 * What an officeholder produces by acting -- the Clerk certifying minutes,
 * the Zoning Officer attesting an inspection. `documentHash` is what was
 * certified, not the document itself: a VC is signed and meant to be
 * shared, and the document it attests to may not be. The OfficeGrant that
 * authorized this act is not a field here; it belongs in the VC's own
 * `evidence`, a sibling of credentialSubject, since it is evidence *for*
 * this claim rather than part of what is being claimed.
 */
concept Attestation {
  o String id
  o String documentHash
  o String statement
  @description("Which contract this concerns, when it concerns one. A council vote and the minutes approving it are not themselves contract executions -- a proceeding like that has no parties and no mutual assent, so it is not a Contract -- but it usually happens about one.")
  o String contractId optional
  @description("Which matter this concerns, when it concerns one -- for an attestation that moves a document of the matter through its lifecycle")
  o String matterId optional
  @description("When the officeholder actually performed this act -- wall-clock time. Distinct from validFrom on the outer VC envelope, which is the event's own time (the meeting the statement is about), not when it was typed in. The two coincide for a same-day certification and diverge for a Clerk certifying a months-old vote, which is the case this project was built around.")
  o DateTime certifiedAt
}

/**
 * An officeholder appointed, in writing, to act for another on one
 * matter -- the "Director's designated representative" of a construction
 * contract's General Conditions. Issued by the designator to the designee
 * (`id`); the VC's own validFrom/validUntil bound the appointment.
 *
 * Only authority the designator holds can be delegated, and a designee's
 * authority lasts only while the designator still holds it: com.trustblocks.
 * xtdb.certification checks both when the designee acts. A designation is
 * not itself delegable.
 */
concept Designation {
  o String id
  o String name
  @description("The capacity the designee acts in, as the contract names it, e.g. \"Designated Representative of the Director of Public Works\"")
  o String capacity
  @description("The one matter the designation covers")
  o String matterId
  o Authority[] authority
}

/**
 * An agent's advice on a document of a matter -- a summary, an anomaly it
 * noticed, a question for the officeholder who decides. Signed by the
 * agent's own DID, under a Designation for the matter carrying only
 * ADVISE, which is its evidence.
 *
 * Advice, never a determination: an Advisory moves nothing, certifies
 * nothing, and no lifecycle step accepts one. Whether the deadline was
 * missed or the figures agree is the contract's code; what the Town does
 * about it is an officeholder's decision.
 */
concept Advisory {
  o String id
  o String matterId
  @description("The document of the matter it concerns")
  o String contractId
  @description("The stored file it read, when it read one")
  o String documentHash optional
  o String text
  @description("A minimum-review result, 'pass' or 'flag'. Still advice: the officeholder who receives the document decides")
  o String verdict optional
  @description("The questions the minimum review asked")
  o String[] checklist optional
  o DateTime certifiedAt
}

/**
 * An officeholder's certification that a document was received -- the way
 * a party with no identity of its own (a contractor, a consulting engineer,
 * a surety) enters the record: the Town's officeholder vouches for receipt,
 * under her own authority. `documentHash` names the stored file exactly
 * (com.trustblocks.xtdb.document). When it was received is the VC's
 * validFrom; certifiedAt is when she certified it.
 */
concept Receipt {
  o String id
  o String documentHash
  o String matterId
  @description("Who the document was received from, as named on it, e.g. \"Example Paving, LLC\"")
  o String receivedFrom
  o String description optional
  @description("The role the document plays in the matter's package manifest, e.g. \"certificate-of-insurance\"")
  o String documentRole optional
  @description("The document instance whose lifecycle this receipt moved -- a pay request received -- when it moved one")
  o String contractId optional
  o DateTime certifiedAt
}
